Let's expand the powers for $
\left(\blueD{8^n}\right)^{\greenD{3}}=\purpleD{8^6}$.

$\begin{align}
\left(\blueD{8^n}\right)^{\greenD3}&=\underbrace{\blueD{8^n\cdot 8^n \cdot 8^n}}_\greenD{\text{3 times}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{\blueD{8 \cdot 8}}_{n\text{ times}}
\cdot \underbrace{\blueD{8 \cdot 8}}_{n\text{ times}}
 \cdot \underbrace{\blueD{8\cdot 8}}_{n\text{ times}}}
_\greenD{\text{3 times}}
\\\\
&=\purpleD{\underbrace{8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot 8\cdot  8\cdot  8}_\text{6 times}}
\\\\
\end{align}$
